Title: Night Ferry
Author: Draftboard test script
Draft date: Test

INT. FERRY TERMINAL - NIGHT

Fluorescent lights buzz over an empty waiting room. DEE (30s), soaked from the rain, counts crumpled bills on a plastic seat.

A TICKET CLERK (60s) watches her over half-moon glasses.

TICKET CLERK
Last boat's at midnight. After that, nothing till Tuesday.

DEE
Then I'm on the last boat.

She slides the money across. It is not enough. The clerk pushes back two bills.

TICKET CLERK
(quietly)
Pay me when you're back.

EXT. FERRY DECK - NIGHT

Wind and spray. Dee grips the rail as the island lights shrink behind her. Her phone buzzes. A text: "He knows you left."

She drops the phone into the black water.

INT. FERRY CABIN - NIGHT

A cramped cabin. MARCUS (40s), in a good coat that doesn't belong here, sits across from Dee. He smiles like they're old friends.

MARCUS
You threw away a perfectly good phone.

DEE
How did you get on this boat?

MARCUS
Same way you did. I paid.

He sets a photo on the table: a child on a swing.

MARCUS (CONT'D)
She asks about you.

Dee doesn't touch the photo.

EXT. MAINLAND DOCK - NIGHT

The ferry bumps the pilings. Passengers shuffle off. Dee slips between two trucks and runs.

Marcus steps onto the dock behind her, in no hurry at all.

INT. ALL-NIGHT DINER - LATER

Dee slides into a booth. ROSA (50s), a waitress with a pencil behind her ear, pours coffee without asking.

ROSA
You look like a girl who needs pie.

DEE
I need a car.

ROSA
(beat)
Pie first.

INT. DINER - BACK OFFICE - CONTINUOUS

Rosa hands Dee a set of keys from a hook. A faded photo on the wall shows a young Rosa with a child on a swing. The same swing.

DEE
Where did you get this?

ROSA
Same place you did, honey. I left too.

EXT. COASTAL HIGHWAY - DAWN

Dee drives Rosa's old pickup into the sunrise. In the rearview mirror, headlights. Far back, but there.

She presses the gas. The headlights keep pace.

EXT. CLIFFSIDE PULLOUT - DAY

Dee pulls over. The headlights pull in behind her. Marcus gets out, hands up, the photo in one of them.

MARCUS
I'm not here to take you back.

DEE
Then why are you here?

MARCUS
Because she's sick. And you're the only match.

Dee looks at the photo, then at the sea. Long silence.

DEE
Get in.

FADE OUT.
